{"author":{"id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyMTA5NDkz","is_bot":false,"login":"td72","name":"Kohei Hosokawa"},"body":"## Summary\nvig polls GitHub through `gh` (workflow runs every 5 s while active, PR checks watch, running-job log polls, board loads). A busy session can exhaust the 5,000 req/h quota, and today `gh` errors are just displayed as fetch failures.\n\n## Tasks\n- [ ] Detect rate-limit errors in `gh` output (REST and GraphQL messages); on detection, exponentially back off all polling and show `⚠ GitHub rate limited (resets in Nm)` in the status bar — the reset time comes from `gh api rate_limit` (that endpoint is not rate-limited)\n- [ ] Make poll intervals configurable: top-level `github-poll-interval` (default 5 s, floor 2 s) used by the runs watch, checks watch and log polls\n- [ ] Audit that no polling continues while its page is inactive (log polls, board refresh); make startup refetches conditional where a disk cache exists\n- [ ] docs/config.md + tests (error detection, backoff progression, interval validation)","comments":[],"createdAt":"2026-08-31T06:07:22Z","labels":[{"id":"LA_kwDORNPWJs8AAAACXrzvTg","name":"enhancement","description":"New feature or request","color":"a2eeef"}],"number":135,"state":"CLOSED","title":"GitHub polling: rate-limit awareness and backoff"}
